WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.368
-My first guest
is a talented actor,

00:00:02.368 --> 00:00:03.970
who you can see
in the new movie "Freaky,"

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:05.871
which is in theaters
this Friday.

00:00:05.871 --> 00:00:09.743
Here he is, Vince Vaughn.
Vince, oh --

00:00:09.743 --> 00:00:11.543
-Good to see you, man.
-I'm so happy.

00:00:11.543 --> 00:00:13.646
Thank you so much
for doing this.

00:00:13.646 --> 00:00:15.448
I really appreciate it.
-Always great to see you, dude.

00:00:15.448 --> 00:00:17.816
-Yeah, great.
Last time you helped me out,

00:00:17.816 --> 00:00:19.251
it was six months ago.

00:00:19.251 --> 00:00:21.487
We were on Zoom, and we're like,
"What's going on?"

00:00:21.487 --> 00:00:23.756
We're trying to help each other
out with our kids and stuff.

00:00:23.756 --> 00:00:25.725
Here we are,
we're still on Zoom.

00:00:25.725 --> 00:00:27.527
-I know.
We're still in the middle of it.

00:00:27.527 --> 00:00:28.961
-Yeah.
-But you're back in the studio,

00:00:28.961 --> 00:00:31.030
which is exciting.
-Yeah. This is exciting.

00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:32.464
It's good.
It's baby steps.

00:00:32.464 --> 00:00:34.833
It's very safe here at NBC.
[ Ringtone plays ]

00:00:34.833 --> 00:00:37.570
-Are you liking that?
-Wait. That's me calling you.

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:39.272
-Hello, Jimmy?
I got you.

00:00:39.272 --> 00:00:40.873
You're right here on Zoom.
Thank you so much.

00:00:40.873 --> 00:00:42.742
-Okay, I'll talk to you later.

00:00:42.742 --> 00:00:45.344
-Are you liking
being back in the studio?

00:00:45.344 --> 00:00:47.547
-Yeah, I am.
I do like it here.

00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:51.083
It's -- I miss the audience,
and I miss

00:00:51.083 --> 00:00:52.619
having all the writers around.

00:00:52.619 --> 00:00:55.688
And, you know,
everyone's so spaced out.

00:00:55.688 --> 00:00:57.289
They're in different
little things.

00:00:57.289 --> 00:00:59.192
Not all the writers
can come back.

00:00:59.192 --> 00:01:01.227
So it's a little tough that way.

00:01:01.227 --> 00:01:03.929
But besides that, I like --

00:01:03.929 --> 00:01:06.899
The sound is much better.
My kids aren't running.

00:01:06.899 --> 00:01:09.134
-I thought you did a great job
from home, and your wife, too.

00:01:09.134 --> 00:01:10.603
You guys did a great job
from home.

00:01:10.603 --> 00:01:12.371
-Thank you.
I feel like my wife --

00:01:12.371 --> 00:01:13.540
-It's probably nice
to get some space,

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:15.207
for her to get a little space
from you.

00:01:15.207 --> 00:01:17.109
-[ Laughs ]
-You can go crank up the funnies

00:01:17.109 --> 00:01:20.246
downtown now, am I right?
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:21.881
I was gonna say,
she's very cool.

00:01:21.881 --> 00:01:23.583
She's like, "No, it was great.

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:25.918
It was just
a perfect amount of time."

00:01:25.918 --> 00:01:28.254
I want to say two weeks ago,
I go, "Honey, I think I can

00:01:28.254 --> 00:01:30.890
probably come home a little
early, you know, if you want."

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:33.592
She goes, "Take your time.
Take the night."

00:01:33.592 --> 00:01:35.528
And then I go, "Okay."

00:01:35.528 --> 00:01:36.829
-A nice way of saying,
it's like,

00:01:36.829 --> 00:01:38.698
"Don't do it for us.
We're okay."

00:01:38.698 --> 00:01:40.800
[ Both laugh ]
-Exactly.

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:43.502
Is remote learning going okay
with you and your kids?

00:01:43.502 --> 00:01:44.771
-Yeah.
It's been good.

00:01:44.771 --> 00:01:47.473
We do pods.
We have four in a class.

00:01:47.473 --> 00:01:48.941
-Yep.
-It's not like I'm

00:01:48.941 --> 00:01:51.277
in the middle of it, like,
rolling up my sleeves.

00:01:51.277 --> 00:01:53.879
I hired a teacher,
which is a benefit for everyone,

00:01:53.879 --> 00:01:55.314
including the children.
-Yeah.

00:01:55.314 --> 00:01:57.217
My wife did that, too, yeah.
-And they're loving it.

00:01:57.217 --> 00:01:59.351
And I like it 'cause at least
they get to socialize, like,

00:01:59.351 --> 00:02:01.654
"Hey, that was my pencil,"
or, you know,

00:02:01.654 --> 00:02:03.122
they're at least
learning how to behave.

00:02:03.122 --> 00:02:04.456
How about you?
You're doing the same thing?

00:02:04.456 --> 00:02:06.025
-Same exact thing.
Yeah.

00:02:06.025 --> 00:02:07.493
Me and my wife
set up this whole thing,

00:02:07.493 --> 00:02:09.762
and it's --
You know, we just didn't know

00:02:09.762 --> 00:02:11.297
where it was gonna go
and what to do,

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:13.099
but the kids
are having a great time.

00:02:13.099 --> 00:02:14.367
They're learning.
It's like we have

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:16.235
all sorts of different teachers,

00:02:16.235 --> 00:02:18.003
music teachers,
Spanish teachers.

00:02:18.003 --> 00:02:21.941
It's like -- I had nothing
like that going to my school.

00:02:21.941 --> 00:02:23.609
-No.
You're, like, raising X-Men.

00:02:23.609 --> 00:02:26.245
That's exciting. You have,
like, music and Spanish?

00:02:26.245 --> 00:02:28.013
-[ Laughing ]
-Like raising

00:02:28.013 --> 00:02:30.483
future Secret Service.
-You know, my kids love is --

00:02:30.483 --> 00:02:33.819
Winnie loves Reading Eggs,
you told me about.

00:02:33.819 --> 00:02:35.288
It's an app.
-Yes.

00:02:35.288 --> 00:02:38.091
My kids have enjoyed that.
-She does that.

00:02:38.091 --> 00:02:40.793
-Do you make them earn games
by doing that?

00:02:40.793 --> 00:02:42.262
-Yep.
Exactly right.

00:02:42.262 --> 00:02:44.497
She's actually, like, going
like, "I've got to read more,

00:02:44.497 --> 00:02:45.998
because I've got
to get the game."

00:02:45.998 --> 00:02:49.468
But I don't know -- the logo
freaks me out a little bit.

00:02:49.468 --> 00:02:51.670
-A little bit?
A lot, yeah, a lot.

00:02:51.670 --> 00:02:54.707
-You see that thing?
-Yeah, it's not a --

00:02:54.707 --> 00:02:57.744
-Is it a human?
-It's a nice app, to be clear,

00:02:57.744 --> 00:03:00.747
but the logo design,
I don't know what happened.

00:03:00.747 --> 00:03:04.083
-It's like a kid
inside of an egg.

00:03:04.083 --> 00:03:06.085
-Bursting out of their egg.

00:03:06.085 --> 00:03:08.655
-That's true.
Bursting out.

00:03:08.655 --> 00:03:11.891
It's much too large.
Already wearing shoes.

00:03:11.891 --> 00:03:14.126
And then, like,
throwing a plane --

00:03:14.126 --> 00:03:15.595
I don't know.
I think I would go back...

00:03:15.595 --> 00:03:18.531
-I'd like to see it with you and
myself bursting out of the egg.

00:03:18.531 --> 00:03:20.766
That could be an exciting logo.
-Yeah.

00:03:20.766 --> 00:03:23.869
We don't have an investment
in this company,

00:03:23.869 --> 00:03:26.239
but why not us coming out,
like, holding --

00:03:26.239 --> 00:03:27.673
Or even holding books
or something.

00:03:27.673 --> 00:03:30.976
Why a plane?
-Yeah, right.

00:03:30.976 --> 00:03:34.446
Why not engage in reading?

00:03:34.446 --> 00:03:38.251
-Have you watched movies
with the kids?

00:03:38.251 --> 00:03:40.052
-I do.
I watch a lot of movies,

00:03:40.052 --> 00:03:43.288
and my son has a real appetite
for dangerous stuff.

00:03:43.288 --> 00:03:44.590
And he's 7 years old.

00:03:44.590 --> 00:03:46.092
I watched the original
"Dirty Harry" with him.

00:03:46.092 --> 00:03:48.094
I don't know how this plays out,
but I did it.

00:03:48.094 --> 00:03:50.095
-Wow!
-I know. It's scary.

00:03:50.095 --> 00:03:51.530
It's freaky.
You remember that guy

00:03:51.530 --> 00:03:53.165
that's a real psycho
in that movie?

00:03:53.165 --> 00:03:55.033
-Yeah, he's like --
It's, like, awful.

00:03:55.033 --> 00:03:56.802
-Remember, he's, like,
shooting people from a rooftop

00:03:56.802 --> 00:03:58.003
to open up the film?

00:03:58.003 --> 00:03:59.672
-And he's, like,
laughing really --

00:03:59.672 --> 00:04:01.374
[ Laughter ]

00:04:01.374 --> 00:04:02.709
Oh, that's scary to me.

00:04:02.709 --> 00:04:04.443
My little one
likes the scary ones.

00:04:04.443 --> 00:04:07.179
She likes those --
like, we watched "Coraline"

00:04:07.179 --> 00:04:09.382
and thought she was going to
freak out, and she loved it.

00:04:09.382 --> 00:04:10.950
-"Coraline's" a scary one.
-She's like,

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:12.018
"Why does everyone
have button eyes?"

00:04:12.018 --> 00:04:13.486
-When the eyes go away.
-Yeah, she goes,

00:04:13.486 --> 00:04:14.587
"Do you and Mommy
have button eyes?"

00:04:14.587 --> 00:04:15.922
And I go, "Okay, all right."

00:04:15.922 --> 00:04:17.990
Let's go back
to watching cartoons.

00:04:17.990 --> 00:04:19.658
-Sometimes it goes over
their head, thankfully.

00:04:19.658 --> 00:04:22.094
-What were you watching
when you were their age?

00:04:22.094 --> 00:04:26.599
-I had two older sisters, so
they weren't knocking to go see,

00:04:26.599 --> 00:04:28.934
you know, "Jaws"
or "Saturday Night Fever"

00:04:28.934 --> 00:04:30.069
just 'cause I was like 6.

00:04:30.069 --> 00:04:31.904
So I would go --
I was like --

00:04:31.904 --> 00:04:34.073
They'd just, like,
"Bring him along."

00:04:34.073 --> 00:04:36.308
But I kind of liked --
I didn't like scary.

00:04:36.308 --> 00:04:38.343
Scary really bothered me
at night. You?

00:04:38.343 --> 00:04:40.847
-Yeah, no, I was not a scary --

00:04:40.847 --> 00:04:42.482
I don't think
I was even allowed to.

00:04:42.482 --> 00:04:44.116
We didn't have HBO.
We had nothing.

00:04:44.116 --> 00:04:47.319
So, I mean, if I did see
a horror movie, it was like --

00:04:47.319 --> 00:04:50.256
Oh, gosh, maybe some edited
version of "Halloween"

00:04:50.256 --> 00:04:51.657
or something on TV.

00:04:51.657 --> 00:04:53.325
-Inappropriate language
and that kind of stuff --

00:04:53.325 --> 00:04:55.928
the comedy stuff
I was fine with.

00:04:55.928 --> 00:04:58.197
-We were --
-Possession stuff bothered me.

00:04:58.197 --> 00:04:59.799
The puppets talking and stuff

00:04:59.799 --> 00:05:01.067
would really give me
a hard evening.

00:05:01.067 --> 00:05:03.202
-Yeah, I agree.
The "Twilight Zone"

00:05:03.202 --> 00:05:04.670
with the puppet,
where he talks back,

00:05:04.670 --> 00:05:06.172
and the guy becomes the puppet.

00:05:06.172 --> 00:05:08.574
-Wasn't it "Twilight Zone"
with Burgess Meredith,

00:05:08.574 --> 00:05:10.242
the gentleman who dazzled
in "Rocky,"

00:05:10.242 --> 00:05:11.911
when he lost his glasses?

00:05:11.911 --> 00:05:14.179
-He's -- The man loves books.

00:05:14.179 --> 00:05:16.248
-Yes, that's it.
-He loves to read,

00:05:16.248 --> 00:05:18.851
and it's the end of the world,
and he's the only --

00:05:18.851 --> 00:05:21.453
And he survives,
and he goes over to the library

00:05:21.453 --> 00:05:23.856
and just rubble
and thousands of books,

00:05:23.856 --> 00:05:26.326
and he's like...
[ Laughing ]

00:05:26.326 --> 00:05:28.427
Like, crazy laughing,
he's so happy.

00:05:28.427 --> 00:05:30.529
And he walks, and he trips,
and his glasses fall off,

00:05:30.529 --> 00:05:33.299
and he breaks his glasses.
-Yeah.

00:05:33.299 --> 00:05:35.734
They did a nice job
with that show, didn't they?

00:05:35.734 --> 00:05:38.236
-Oh, they were so good.
I remember the first movie

00:05:38.236 --> 00:05:41.039
I think my parents took me to,
I was probably 5 or 6,

00:05:41.039 --> 00:05:44.043
I saw "The Champ,"
with Ricky Schroeder.

00:05:44.043 --> 00:05:48.047
-Did the tears fall?
-Dude, I cried my eyes out.

00:05:48.047 --> 00:05:50.382
Everyone was crying.
It's unbelievable.

00:05:50.382 --> 00:05:53.453
You don't take a kid to go see
"The Champ," do you?

00:05:53.453 --> 00:05:55.254
-That was a remake.
I didn't realize that,

00:05:55.254 --> 00:05:58.024
but there was
an original "Champ."

00:05:58.024 --> 00:06:00.926
Was the same actor from
"Treasure Island."

00:06:00.926 --> 00:06:03.863
Did you always watch movies?
Were you always into movies?

00:06:03.863 --> 00:06:05.631
-Yeah, my parents loved --
-Yeah, me, too.

00:06:05.631 --> 00:06:07.800
-Yeah, loved it.
We were Irish Catholic,

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:09.802
so every James Cagney movie --
We were watching

00:06:09.802 --> 00:06:11.637
gangster movies,
didn't know what they were.

00:06:11.637 --> 00:06:14.040
-Would your dad go around the
house saying, "You dirty rat"?

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:16.675
-Yeah, that was
my first impression.

00:06:16.675 --> 00:06:18.210
I swear I'll get it next time
you're on.

00:06:18.210 --> 00:06:20.212
I'm gonna play it for you.
I was probably 2 years old.

00:06:20.212 --> 00:06:23.148
I said, "You dirty rat."
-It's so good.

00:06:23.148 --> 00:06:25.217
Would you go to school
and say that to people,

00:06:25.217 --> 00:06:27.019
and they were like, "Where is
this guy coming from?"

00:06:27.019 --> 00:06:31.056
-I was doing, like, Don Ho
impressions like, no one --

00:06:31.056 --> 00:06:32.692
-You were singing
"Tiny Bubbles"?

00:06:32.692 --> 00:06:34.994
-I said aloha.
That was my jam.

00:06:34.994 --> 00:06:38.197
No, that wasn't the opener,
nor was it a closer.

00:06:38.197 --> 00:06:40.566
But it was somewhere in the act.
-Yeah.

